Research: .collab/research/2026-10-16-t3-code-c2c-support.md and live receipt JSON. Quality: preserve existing codebase architecture; small typed interfaces; meaningful regression and failure tests; no mock-only delivery claims; no whole-tree refactor; independent review/fix loop before merge. Decisions and evidence must be appended through bl. Define concrete per-environment/T3-thread identity, generation, broker location, structured envelope, selected-ID acknowledgment, offline retention, ephemeral/deferrable/DND semantics, and failure receipt states. Assign c2c vs T3 ownership. Audit existing broker/ack APIs and T3 architecture before new abstraction. Record exact cross-repo contract and file-overlap lane plan; implementable without deciding protocol in worker code.

Decision: implementation contract is .collab/design/2026-10-17-t3-host-mailbox-contract.md. c2c host transport reuses broker primitives, preserves durable source provenance, and fences commands by generation. T3 storage and provider interfaces are disjoint lanes; lifecycle/config/scheduler wiring is serial after foundation merges. Host mode is explicit, native provider c2c consumers suppressed uniformly, no per-thread identity env in shared runtime. Codex first; unsupported adapters remain explicit. Existing source and independent seam reviews resolve design. No broad refactors; strict DATA and quality gates.